@startuml
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title Shared Bus Control Register (Offset 0E0h)

package "Register Layout" {
  rectangle "D31" as D31
  rectangle "D30-D24\n\nBack-End Power\nControl" as D30_24 #LightGray
  rectangle "D23" as D23
  rectangle "D22-D20\n\nInterrupt Pin Select" as D22_20 #LightGray
  rectangle "D19" as D19
  rectangle "D18-D16\n\nClock Pin Select" as D18_16 #LightGray
  rectangle "D15" as D15
  rectangle "D14-D08\n\nBus Width Preset" as D14_08 #LightGray
  rectangle "D07-D06" as D07_06
  rectangle "D05-D04\n\nNumber of Interrupt\nInput Pins" as D05_04 #LightGray
  rectangle "D03" as D03
  rectangle "D02-D00\n\nNumber of Clock Pins" as D02_00 #LightGray
  
  D31 -[hidden]right- D30_24
  D30_24 -[hidden]right- D23
  D23 -[hidden]right- D22_20
  D22_20 -[hidden]right- D19
  D19 -[hidden]right- D18_16
  D18_16 -[hidden]right- D15
  D15 -[hidden]right- D14_08
  D14_08 -[hidden]right- D07_06
  D07_06 -[hidden]right- D05_04
  D05_04 -[hidden]right- D03
  D03 -[hidden]right- D02_00
}

note bottom of "Register Layout"
  **Figure 2-37: Shared Bus Control Register**
end note

rectangle "Field Details" {
  
  card "**D31: Reserved (Rsvd)**" as F31
  
  card "**D30-24: Back-End Power Control (RW)**\n\nEach bit controls back-end power supply for an embedded device.\nHost interface voltage (VDDH) is not controlled by this field.\nNumber of devices supported is specified by **Number of Clock Pins**\nand a maximum of 7 devices can be controlled.\n\n**Bit Assignments:**\n• D16: Back-end Power Control for Device 1\n• D17: Back-end Power Control for Device 2\n• D18: Back-end Power Control for Device 3\n• D19: Back-end Power Control for Device 4\n• D20: Back-end Power Control for Device 5\n• D21: Back-end Power Control for Device 6\n• D22: Back-end Power Control for Device 7\n\n**Values:**\n• 0: Back-end Power is Off\n• 1: Back-end Power is Supplied\n\nBack-End power control is effective for embedded memory devices in the\nSleep State that support the Sleep command (CMD14) to reduce power\nconsumption and embedded SDIO devices when IOEx is set to 0." as F30_24
  
  card "**D23: Reserved (Rsvd)**" as F23
  
  card "**D22-20: Interrupt Pin Select (RW)**\n\nInterrupt pin inputs are enabled by this field.\nEnable of unsupported interrupt pin is meaningless.\n\n**Values:**\n• 000b: Interrupt is detected by Interrupt Cycle\n• xx1b: INT_A is Enabled\n• x1xb: INT_B is Enabled\n• 1xxb: INT_C is Enabled" as F22_20
  
  card "**D19: Reserved (Rsvd)**" as F19
}

F31 -[hidden]down- F30_24
F30_24 -[hidden]down- F23
F23 -[hidden]down- F22_20
F22_20 -[hidden]down- F19

@enduml